  "name": "bantaML",
  "description": "A high-performance Standard ML and Lisp implementation leveraging a Rust-based runtime with C-interoperability. The system features a custom bytecode interpreter or tree-walking evaluator with support for first-class continuations, manual memory management via a C-style object model, and an extensible builtin system using procedural macros. It appears to be a transcription or port of a C-based Lisp engine (tiny-lisp) into a memory-safe environment with low-level FFIs.",
